  "title": "Week of September 12 Logbook — NVIDIA's Throne, Unshaken",
  "summary": "As NVIDIA holds the Sun's position at $5.27 trillion in market cap, a hot updraft sweeps through the semiconductor sector.",
  "body": "<h3>Stability of the Throne</h3><p>This week, the order of the universe remained unchanged from last week. NVIDIA firmly holds the Sun's seat with a market cap of $5.27 trillion. Apple ($4.85 trillion), Alphabet ($4.1 trillion), Microsoft ($3.68 trillion), and Amazon ($2.77 trillion) follow, with the orbits of the top 5 planets in stable state.</p><h3>Updraft in the Semiconductor Belt</h3><p>What stands out is the weekly gainers ranking. SK Hynix recorded the hottest performance with a gain of 10.5%, followed by AMD (8.1%) and Meta Platforms (5.0%). In particular, the strong rise of South Korean semiconductor company SK Hynix suggests a positive trend across the industry.</p><h3>The Sun's Paradox</h3><p>An interesting observation is NVIDIA's own weakness. This week, NVIDIA posted a decline of 5.2%, ranking first on the weekly losers list. The phenomenon of the Sun holding its throne while simultaneously showing weakness reveals the complex dynamics of the universe. Meanwhile, Micron Technology (-4.1%) and Eli Lilly (-2.8%) also declined.</p><h3>Movements at the Periphery</h3><p>Potential rising candidates like SanDisk (momentum 838), Dell (352), and Seagate Technology (322) are under monitoring. Additionally, Fortinet has been detected as a new observation target. The trajectories these planets will trace in the future will be confirmed through continued observation.</p><h3>Recording in History</h3><p>The order of the universe flows ceaselessly, but the data observed this week is clear. NVIDIA's position as the Sun remained unshaken, a hot wind blows through the semiconductor industry, and the arrangement of top-tier planets is identical to the previous week. The universe turns, and the record remains.</p><div class=\"col-chart\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 700 310\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><defs><linearGradient id=\"wg2\" x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"1\" y2=\"0\"><stop offset=\"0%\" stop-color=\"#9c7a3a\"/><stop offset=\"100%\" stop-color=\"#f2ba3c\"/></li